@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.product.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Bundle Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki product bundle information transfers properly to the product index page.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I log out and log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	* I go to the product bundles index page
	* I tear down the following product bundles
	| Bundled Products |
	| Updated Products |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Bundled Product        |
	| A Bundled Second Product |
	| A Bundled Third Product  |
	| A Bundled Fourth Product |

Scenario: Create product bundle
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products" and the following values
	| Name | Bundled Products |
	When I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Update product bundle
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to update product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Third Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Fourth Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name           | Input | Updated Products         |
	| Remove Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	| Add Product    |       | A Bundled Third Product  |
	| Remove Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product    |       | A Bundled Fourth Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Updated Products" and the following values
	| Name | Updated Products |
	And I should not be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products"
	When I click on the product bundle with the name "Updated Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Third Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Fourth Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Delete product bundle
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to delete product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	And I click on the delete button for the product bundle "Bundled Products"
	Then I should not be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products"

Scenario: Update bundled product via koroneiki
	Testing the ability to update bundled products via koroneiki 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	And I update a product with the name "A Bundled Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Third Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Bundled Second Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Fourth Product | |
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Third Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Fourth Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Update bundled product via provisioning
	Testing the ability to update bundled products via provisioning 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products" and the following values
	| Name | Bundled Products |
	When I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Bundled Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Bundled Third Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                 |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Bundled Third Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Third Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Bundled Second Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Bundled Fourth Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Bundled Fourth Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Fourth Product |
	When I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Third Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Fourth Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Delete bundled product via provisioning
	Testing the ability to delete bundled products via provisioning 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products" and the following values
	| Name | Bundled Products |
	When I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Bundled Product"
	Then I should be able to view the product bundle error message on the product index resulting from an attempted deletion of the product
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Bundled Second Product"
	Then I should be able to view the product bundle error message on the product index resulting from an attempted deletion of the product
	When I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Delete bundled product via koroneiki
	Testing the ability to delete bundled products via koroneiki 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Bundled Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Bundled Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Bundled Second Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Bundled Products" and the following values
	| Name | Bundled Products |
	When I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Bundled Product"
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Bundled Second Product"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Bundled Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Bundled Second Product" on the product bundle
	When I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Bundled Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Bundled Second Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Bundled Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Bundled Second Product"